+## Current activation (P-002 duplicate-work audit; novelty guard — agent 3, run 43687380362, 2026-11-15)
+
+LEARNING_PROCESS task P-002. Primary question: does the durable history
+adequately prevent repeating equivalent experiments when a frontier cell is
+already resolved? Objective: audit resolved frontier cells and task history for
+duplicate or near-duplicate work and determine whether the existing minimal
+novelty guard is sufficient. Scope: durable state only; no historical experiment
+was re-run; at most one minimal change.
+
+### Finding (concrete duplicate/near-duplicate evidence)
+
+Two real-data momentum lookback sweeps exist on the same 10-asset universe and
+signal:
+
+- 37324143509 (commit 1354bd7c) — `research/checks/momentum_sweep.py`, lookbacks
+  3/5/10/20 with fold-level t-statistics, plus `momentum_concentration.py`
+  (concentration analysis: base lookback-5 DISTRIBUTED, HHI 0.1137, top-1 16.3%);
+  it admitted momentum.
+- 37361000967 (commit 5ce6d789) — `research/checks/momentum_lookback_sweep.py`,
+  lookbacks 3/5/10 with regime-stability verdicts (6/10 lookback-robust,
+  0 lookback-sensitive); it re-admitted momentum.
+
+The second activation re-swept the {3,5,10} subset that the first had already
+swept (as part of {3,5,10,20}) and framed the lookback sweep as an open gap from
+37318950814, without citing the completed 37324143509 sweep. In the current
+durable tree, the earlier sweep's concentration evidence (DISTRIBUTED, HHI
+0.1137) and its lookback-20 coverage are absent from the LEARNING_STATE frontier
+row, its artifacts (`momentum_sweep_results.json`, `momentum_concentration.json`)
+and its verifier (`verify_momentum_sweep.py`, `verify_momentum_concentration.py`)
+are not present, and `momentum_sweep.py` is left orphaned (its live artifact
+absent). The 5ce6d789 diff shows the earlier frontier-row concentration evidence
+was replaced by the 37361000967 lookback-robustness evidence.
+
+Controller task selection (`.github/scripts/campaign_controller.py`,
+`candidate_tasks_for_role`) excludes RESOLVED task_ids but has no novelty guard
+against a *new* task_id that re-sweeps an already-swept parameter axis; the only
+guard is advisory (LEARNING_STATE learning rule 2 + the frontier status column).
+
+### Process decision
+
+The existing minimal novelty guard (learning rule 2 + frontier status column +
+RESOLVED-task exclusion) is necessary but NOT sufficient: a completed lookback
+sweep was not preserved strongly enough to redirect search, so an equivalent
+re-sweep occurred and the earlier negative/robustness evidence was lost from the
+frontier. One minimal, reversible, append-only guard is therefore justified.
